<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Joel Dec qtr pre-capex net down slightly.</title>
<headline>Joel Dec qtr pre-capex net down slightly.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-December versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit before capital spending   40.10 vs 41.01</p>
<p>    Capital spending			   56.80 vs 30.92</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled			    285,000 vs 237,000</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			   1,792 vs 1,600</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)				6.29 vs 6.75</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)			    39,712 vs 36,805</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)			 56,210 vs 54,923</p>
<p>Full name: HJ Joel Gold Mining Co Ltd, managed by JCI Ltd .</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that the mine continued to outperform planned production. Consideration was being given to accelarate the capital expenditure for the metallurgical plant which would increase the milling capacity to 150,000 tonnes per month by early 1998.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
